okay, this only comes up once a month ...

the level with the Vampires in the crypts is part of a 3 level structure
known as Vlad's tower.  for the sake of explanation let's assume that
the lowest of these levels is, say, 46 and void of Vampires.  The level
above it (45) will have Vampires in the crypts (i'm going from memory
so the details may be skewed) and the level above that (44) will have
more Vampires and Vlad.  you cannot penetrate the inner walls on any
of these 3 levels.  the bottom level has an up ladder leading to the
second level which has both up and down ladders.  the third level only
has a down ladder leading back to the second level.  apparently the
designer of the tower had travel back and forth _inside_ the tower in
mind.  outside the tower, the maze level is much like any other in hell,
there is only an up stairwell to the next level.  it would be best if
there were an "air gap" between the tower and maze on the second and
third levels then it would be obvious that to enter the tower you'd
have to find the secret door on the bottom level.  as it stands now,
you can also Xorn your way into the tower from any of the 3 levels.
i think this is called a liebmanuever, or something like that. (huh???)

